# Phase 15: found by actually testing a fresh checkout, not by
# inspection — Windows git's common core.autocrlf=true default converts
# LF to CRLF on checkout, which turns docker/backend-entrypoint.sh's
# shebang into "#!/bin/sh\r", and a Linux container's exec() then reports
# "no such file or directory" (looking for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r"), not a permissions or syntax problem. Shell scripts must
# stay LF regardless of who clones this repo or what their global git
# config does.
*.sh text eol=lf
